{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>For</b>, <b>goes out</b> — for He was in the sanctuary of His holiness, and these are the heavens; therefore, <b>and He will come down</b>. The sense of this passage is to bring His decrees, in the manner of David's song, as I have explained." "Some say: <b>among the plantations of the earth</b> — an allusion to the rulers, and likewise: <b>and the mountains will melt</b>, and there is no need. Rather, the sense is: for in all He rules, and He does His will, and the mountains melt at His pleasure."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:32.628004368Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}